    {
      "document_id": "2382",
      "label": "1",
      "explanation": "Although the text begins by describing the introduction of a bill (S. 1588), it explicitly claims credit for a successful casework intervention: 'By intervening with the Department of Homeland Security and removing bureaucratic red tape, Sen. Landrieu recently ensured that Rayan... was able to come... to the United States for treatment.' This fits clarification (c) regarding successful casework interventions helping individuals cut through red tape."
