      "label": "0",
      "explanation": "Senator McCaskill announces the Senate's passage of S. 4 and her amendment. However, the text notes that the bill must still proceed to a conference committee to work out differences with the House, meaning a final positive outcome of the bill becoming law has not yet been secured, falling under negative clarification (b)."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "2827",
      "label": "0",
      "explanation": "This is an Op-Ed by Senator Lieberman discussing the war on terror and the situation in Iraq. It is entirely focused on national security policy and position-taking, which is excluded under negative clarification (a)."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "964",
      "label": "0",
      "explanation": "This press release describes Senators Landrieu and Kerry writing a letter to the Small Business Administration requesting future action. Under negative clarification (c), writing letters to agencies asking for future action does not constitute credit-claiming."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "3149",
      "label": "0",
      "explanation": "Senator Reed discusses the passage of a budget resolution, which is a non-binding spending blueprint rather than a final law allocating funds. Furthermore, he indicates that he will propose future legislation and looks forward to working on appropriations bills, meaning the final outcome has not yet been secured under negative clarification (b)."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "2697",
      "label": "1",
      "explanation": "Senator Inouye announces $225,000 in federal funding to contain coqui frogs on the Big Island and explicitly claims credit for securing these funds by stating that after a request was denied, he 'went looking and found another federal funding source.' This fits clarification (a) perfectly."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "4403",
      "label": "0",
      "explanation": "Senator Domenici announces his cosponsorship and the introduction of the Craig Thomas Rural Hospital and Provider Equity Act of 2007. Since this is the introduction of a bill that has not yet passed, it is excluded under negative clarification (b)."
